WEBVTT

00:19.390 --> 00:23.090
<i>Gokusen</i>

00:23.360 --> 00:28.590
<i>How long has it been</i>
<i>since that day when we first met?</i>

00:28.760 --> 00:34.290
<i>So many good times and bad times</i>
<i>have come and gone since then.</i>

00:34.470 --> 00:39.630
<i>I know you can't make sense</i>
<i>of what I'm trying to say.</i>

00:39.810 --> 00:45.080
<i>But my true feelings for you</i>
<i>can never be put into words.</i>

00:45.380 --> 00:50.820
<i>Will you ever know how I feel?</i>
<i>Will you know what's going on inside me?</i>

00:51.020 --> 00:56.460
<i>If only we could live in a world where</i>
<i>you only have to be yourself and smile.</i>

00:56.620 --> 01:01.890
<i>Or is it always going to be like this?</i>
<i>Will we be able to go on like this?</i>

01:02.100 --> 01:09.800
<i>Even if you're far away, I want to</i>
<i>feel you in my heart, close to me.</i>

01:30.790 --> 01:31.820
What's up?

01:31.960 --> 01:32.950
You need to crap?

01:34.030 --> 01:38.300
Night patrol is an time-honored task.

01:38.470 --> 01:42.430
I've got my eyes peeled, so
you have nothing to worry about.

01:43.740 --> 01:44.640
What's that?

01:44.840 --> 01:46.270
Thief!

01:46.540 --> 01:47.770
Thief?

01:54.850 --> 01:57.480
What the hell?
Don't scare me like that.

01:57.850 --> 01:58.880
Hold it.

01:59.050 --> 01:59.990
Huh?

02:03.020 --> 02:07.990
<i>OJOU GOES BLOND! WHODUNNIT?</i>

02:08.330 --> 02:09.920
What the hell?

02:10.160 --> 02:12.930
Minoru and Fuji got pinched by the cops?

02:13.070 --> 02:15.760
Well, actually Fuji
was just there with him.

02:15.870 --> 02:16.930
It doesn't matter!

02:17.140 --> 02:19.800
Purse-snatching?
They must really have it in for him!

02:19.910 --> 02:22.930
Wakamatsu, Tetsu,
we're going to bring them home!

02:23.080 --> 02:24.070
Yes, Ojou.

02:27.680 --> 02:28.510
Ojou.

02:28.680 --> 02:30.120
Wait a minute.

02:30.850 --> 02:31.840
What?

02:32.120 --> 02:33.820
Are you trying to stop me, Kyo-san?

02:33.920 --> 02:37.220
Well, no. You see, Minoru has
been bailed out by Shinohara...

02:39.590 --> 02:42.650
Ojou, didn't mean to make you worry.

02:42.900 --> 02:43.730
Minoru!

02:43.930 --> 02:44.900
Fuji!

02:45.070 --> 02:49.130
Ojou, I'm ashamed I let
this happen on my watch.

02:51.440 --> 02:54.570
Consigliere, thank you
for taking care of them.

02:54.680 --> 02:56.370
Oh, don't mention it.

02:56.510 --> 02:58.450
They had no proof whatsoever.

02:58.580 --> 03:00.980
I could have given them a hard time...

03:01.150 --> 03:03.880
But I thought it would be better
to let them save face this time.

03:04.020 --> 03:05.420
Thank you very much.

03:06.050 --> 03:10.890
Consigliere, can I offer you
a drink for your trouble?

03:11.130 --> 03:14.530
Thanks, but I have some
urgent business elsewhere.

03:14.630 --> 03:16.890
Kumiko, is the
teaching job going well?

03:17.200 --> 03:19.030
Um, yes!

03:19.700 --> 03:20.900
Keep up the good work.

03:21.270 --> 03:22.760
Well, then, good night.

03:22.900 --> 03:25.000
Thanks very much, Consigliere!

03:29.280 --> 03:31.070
Good night.

03:31.210 --> 03:33.770
Oh, Mr. Shinohara!

03:33.880 --> 03:36.180
Please, take me away from here.

03:36.620 --> 03:38.520
Take me right now, right here!

03:38.790 --> 03:40.220
Grrr!

03:45.490 --> 03:47.930
<i>BEWARE</i>
<i>PURSE-SNATCHER ATLARGE</i>

03:53.330 --> 03:54.960
What's the big idea?

03:55.940 --> 04:00.370
All those posters plastered
all over the school walls!

04:00.610 --> 04:04.570
They're practically implying that
the thief is someone from this school!

04:04.680 --> 04:07.110
Actually, that is what they're saying.

04:07.280 --> 04:08.440
Blatantly!

04:08.850 --> 04:12.050
Well, there's been five incidents
in the past week.

04:12.250 --> 04:14.020
The victims were all elderly.

04:14.160 --> 04:15.620
Well, that's just outrageous!

04:15.760 --> 04:16.920
There's no one here...

04:17.060 --> 04:19.320
And how can you be so sure of that?

04:20.160 --> 04:21.390
Look at the sketch...

04:21.560 --> 04:23.960
There's no question
that this is a youth.

04:24.170 --> 04:28.930
Not only that, but all of the incidents
have occurred near this school.

04:29.100 --> 04:32.470
There isn't one iota of proof that
it isn't a student from this school.

04:32.710 --> 04:34.640
But, but still...

04:34.940 --> 04:38.970
There's also no proof that
it is a student from this school.

04:39.180 --> 04:43.710
Ms. Yamaguchi, you still have
a lot to learn about this place.

04:43.880 --> 04:47.410
There's a world of circumstantial
evidence right here under our noses...

04:47.520 --> 04:48.820
Here in this school...

04:51.030 --> 04:54.260
Thank you for stopping by.

04:58.630 --> 05:01.260
The principal had visitors?

05:01.400 --> 05:04.530
I wonder what's going on
so early in the morning...

05:07.240 --> 05:09.270
Ms. Yamaguchi, what are you doing?

05:09.410 --> 05:10.780
Oh, uh...

05:11.210 --> 05:13.840
They're detectives from the
Shirokin Police Department.

05:13.950 --> 05:15.780
They must've come here
because of the incidents.

05:15.880 --> 05:17.350
Ha, I knew they were cops!

05:18.750 --> 05:19.980
Attention, everyone!

05:20.090 --> 05:22.490
I've just been given some bad news.

05:22.590 --> 05:25.560
The purse-snatcher has claimed
his first casualty last night.

05:26.830 --> 05:29.590
The thief struck an old woman in the
head with a blunt instrument...

05:29.700 --> 05:31.560
...and ran off with her purse.

05:31.670 --> 05:35.260
Although it's not life-threatening,
the victim remains in critical condition.

05:35.540 --> 05:40.000
So the police are fingering
our students, is that right?

05:40.210 --> 05:42.230
It's true that they're under suspicion...

05:42.340 --> 05:46.870
But there isn't one person in this school
who would stoop to such a heinous act!

05:47.010 --> 05:49.110
At least I don't think so.
I don't think.

05:49.180 --> 05:49.740
Right?

05:49.920 --> 05:51.480
How can you be so naive...

05:51.590 --> 05:55.610
The students abuse your trust
because you take this lenient stance!

05:55.720 --> 05:59.520
We must act now, or there
will be irreparable damage!

06:04.600 --> 06:06.120
But...

06:06.330 --> 06:09.960
Nobody in my class would
ever hit an elderly person.

06:10.240 --> 06:13.900
Well, I don't see anyone
from mine doing that, either.

06:14.040 --> 06:18.170
The little punks in my class would
never do such a hateful thing.

06:18.350 --> 06:19.340
Mine wouldn't either!

06:19.450 --> 06:21.540
Of course, neither would mine!

06:22.550 --> 06:26.750
The teachers all have their complaints,
but they really do care, don't they!

06:28.490 --> 06:30.750
Well, out of all the classes
that should be above suspicion...

06:30.860 --> 06:33.450
...Class 4 is the last one
I'd pin the incidents on!

06:34.330 --> 06:37.260
Man, look at all this cash!

06:37.770 --> 06:39.760
That woman's loaded!

06:43.300 --> 06:45.270
Let's get something after school!
I'm buying!

06:45.370 --> 06:46.930
Are you sure?

06:47.940 --> 06:50.540
The criminal hit an
old woman in the head...

06:50.640 --> 06:53.770
...with a blunt instrument
and made off with her purse.

06:54.880 --> 06:56.440
Goddammit...

06:57.080 --> 06:58.550
Noda!

06:58.690 --> 06:59.240
Huh?

07:07.960 --> 07:09.990
Where'd you get that purse?

07:10.200 --> 07:12.360
You mean this one?

07:12.500 --> 07:14.130
That's a woman's purse.

07:14.300 --> 07:15.200
That's right.

07:15.300 --> 07:17.000
It's my sister's.

07:17.400 --> 07:18.000
What?

07:18.240 --> 07:20.940
I just found it in my bag.

07:21.110 --> 07:24.010
She probably put it in there by mistake.

07:24.280 --> 07:25.080
Huh?

07:25.180 --> 07:27.240
You got a problem with
this purse or something?

07:27.350 --> 07:30.110
No, um...

07:31.090 --> 07:33.180
I just meant that even
if it's your own sister...

07:33.290 --> 07:36.120
...it isn't right to just use her
money without her permission.

07:36.260 --> 07:37.090
Got that?

07:37.220 --> 07:38.890
What? That's it?

07:39.460 --> 07:40.760
Time for class!

07:40.930 --> 07:41.920
Hold it.

07:42.060 --> 07:43.000
Yankumi...

07:43.300 --> 07:47.130
You thought that Noda
was the thief, didn't you?

07:48.770 --> 07:50.100
What?

07:50.640 --> 07:51.800
That's low.

07:51.970 --> 07:53.960
You suspect us, don't you?

07:54.110 --> 07:55.970
And you're supposed to be
our homeroom teacher!

07:56.080 --> 07:57.170
Of course not!

07:57.380 --> 07:59.040
I don't suspect you guys at all.

07:59.180 --> 08:00.610
I believe in you.

08:00.710 --> 08:01.740
Liar!

08:01.880 --> 08:03.820
It was written all over your face.

08:05.420 --> 08:07.450
You're just like everyone else.

08:07.550 --> 08:10.890
Those posters are plastered everywhere.

08:11.030 --> 08:13.090
Everyone thinks it's one of us.

08:13.230 --> 08:15.720
They think we're good for it
even though we didn't do anything!

08:15.830 --> 08:17.590
That really hurts, you know!

08:17.930 --> 08:21.130
If our homeroom teacher doesn't believe
in us, what are we supposed to do?

08:24.040 --> 08:25.370
Just so you know...

08:25.470 --> 08:30.270
Some of us might shoplift from time to time,
but we would never hit an old lady!

08:30.410 --> 08:32.140
Shut up about the shoplifting!

08:32.510 --> 08:33.810
I know.

08:34.180 --> 08:38.780
I know what it feels like to be
pissed off because people suspect you...

08:39.520 --> 08:40.720
I'm sorry.

08:50.960 --> 08:52.260
Goddammit!

08:52.670 --> 08:54.660
Friggin' everyone suspects us.

08:55.200 --> 09:00.160
Yankumi's acting like that because
she thinks we might have done it.

09:00.440 --> 09:03.470
Even the old man at the
bakery behind the school...

09:03.610 --> 09:06.140
When I come by, he ran off
and hid in the back!

09:06.250 --> 09:10.080
That sketch is so general,
it could be any one of us!

09:10.250 --> 09:13.240
Come to think of it,
it does look like you, Noda.

09:13.490 --> 09:14.250
Crap!

09:14.590 --> 09:15.920
You traitor!

09:16.020 --> 09:17.010
Shit.

09:17.120 --> 09:18.680
If everyone suspects us anyway...

09:18.760 --> 09:20.890
...we might as well go out
and snatch some purses!

09:20.990 --> 09:22.690
Hey, Minami...

09:22.800 --> 09:23.560
I'm sorry!

09:23.660 --> 09:25.030
I can't hear you!

09:25.570 --> 09:26.530
Hey!

09:26.730 --> 09:28.070
I have an idea.

09:28.200 --> 09:29.430
Okay, listen up.

09:29.540 --> 09:30.230
What?

09:30.370 --> 09:33.810
Your ideas always end up in disaster.

09:34.240 --> 09:35.440
I don't want to hear it.

09:35.540 --> 09:37.670
Shin-chan's not here today.

09:37.910 --> 09:41.440
Whenever we do something on
our own, it always backfires!

09:43.480 --> 09:45.890
Just shut up and listen!

09:54.700 --> 09:56.860
Hey, cool it, will you?

09:56.960 --> 09:58.330
I know, I know.

09:58.470 --> 10:00.460
Jeez, why's Kuma so late?

10:00.700 --> 10:01.430
Huh?

10:01.600 --> 10:02.630
What is it?

10:02.840 --> 10:04.900
You really do look like that guy.

10:06.540 --> 10:07.800
Hey man!

10:11.210 --> 10:13.810
Hey! What's going on over there?

10:16.150 --> 10:17.680
Wait a minute. You're...

10:17.790 --> 10:19.220
Crap! Run for it!

10:25.030 --> 10:25.820
Noda!

10:26.190 --> 10:27.180
Minami!

10:36.340 --> 10:38.240
What the hell?

10:38.440 --> 10:41.240
Noda and Minami got
picked up by the cops?

10:42.780 --> 10:45.750
<i>Shirokin Police Station</i>

10:53.890 --> 10:54.980
Yankumi.

10:57.490 --> 10:59.720
What happened? Spit it out!

11:00.490 --> 11:02.730
You're acting scary, Yankumi.

11:08.870 --> 11:10.270
What the hell?

11:10.640 --> 11:12.630
You were trying to capture the thief?

11:12.770 --> 11:15.940
Minami came up with the idea because
it sucked that everyone was blaming us...

11:16.040 --> 11:17.380
...and then Noda joined in.

11:17.510 --> 11:19.980
And I thought it sounded kinda fun...

11:20.410 --> 11:24.220
So you were walking around at night,
and they got pinched?

11:24.380 --> 11:28.480
I called Shin right away,
and he told me to call you.

11:28.820 --> 11:29.980
Why?

11:31.230 --> 11:32.660
A gut feeling.

11:32.790 --> 11:34.420
You made the right call, kid!

11:34.600 --> 11:35.490
Stop it.

11:39.500 --> 11:42.830
We're bringing them home,
no matter what it takes.

11:43.000 --> 11:45.230
Okay you cugines, come with me!

11:46.340 --> 11:48.330
Can't you just go in
like a normal person?

11:48.510 --> 11:50.740
You're playing another one
of your roles, aren't you!

11:51.850 --> 11:55.250
So you're asking us to release
those kids we just brought in?

11:55.820 --> 11:57.750
Are you partners with those thieves?

11:58.020 --> 11:59.210
What did you say?

11:59.350 --> 12:01.080
Just try saying that again!

12:01.190 --> 12:04.350
Shut up. Don't mess with the Okami.

12:04.890 --> 12:06.260
Okami?

12:06.560 --> 12:08.650
Oh, I'm sorry!

12:08.800 --> 12:12.060
I'm their homeroom teacher, Yamaguchi.

12:12.200 --> 12:13.630
<i>First Investigation Division</i>

12:13.730 --> 12:15.600
Teacher, huh?

12:16.000 --> 12:18.700
Don't tell me you actually
believe those kids' drivel...

12:18.810 --> 12:21.600
...about trying to
catch the real criminal?

12:21.710 --> 12:23.200
Drivel?

12:24.780 --> 12:27.540
Guv'nor, you don't know
what you're talking about.

12:27.650 --> 12:29.840
These kids don't lie.

12:33.520 --> 12:37.360
You shouldn't let your students
walk all over you like this.

12:38.690 --> 12:40.990
Swallowing their lies...

12:41.430 --> 12:43.190
You can't be so gullible.

12:43.300 --> 12:45.890
Your school's reputation
is in tatters as it is...

12:47.940 --> 12:50.130
What the hell did you just say?

12:51.070 --> 12:52.400
You take that back right now!

12:52.510 --> 12:56.200
If you cops would get your frickin' act
together, we wouldn't be here now!

12:56.310 --> 12:56.900
Uchiyama...

12:57.310 --> 13:00.210
You're not laying a finger
on any of my students....

13:03.250 --> 13:04.620
Calm down, you moron.

13:04.790 --> 13:07.190
What happened to
"Don't mess with the Okami"?

13:09.820 --> 13:12.550
Anyway, you have no proof.

13:12.660 --> 13:14.060
And they're both minors.

13:14.190 --> 13:16.660
So you're just going
to have to release them.

13:17.200 --> 13:19.060
Well, all right, then.

13:19.200 --> 13:21.900
It doesn't mean we're crossing
them off our list of suspects!

13:22.000 --> 13:22.730
Hey!

13:23.040 --> 13:24.500
Bring those two in.

13:24.600 --> 13:25.370
Yes, sir.

13:29.780 --> 13:30.680
Come on!

13:30.780 --> 13:33.010
I was just trying to clear our names.

13:33.150 --> 13:35.270
Yeah, I know.

13:35.420 --> 13:37.280
Never mind that.

13:38.390 --> 13:40.880
But that cop's attitude
really pisses me off!

13:43.060 --> 13:45.860
Ms. Yamaguchi,
what is the meaning of this?

13:46.290 --> 13:49.350
Damn.
That detective squealed on us.

13:49.560 --> 13:51.590
So it's you! Just as I thought.

13:51.700 --> 13:53.530
What do you mean,
just as you thought?

13:53.630 --> 13:54.430
Asshole!

13:54.530 --> 13:55.330
Hold on.

13:56.800 --> 13:57.960
Vice Principal.

13:58.270 --> 14:00.570
This incident was just
a misunderstanding.

14:00.710 --> 14:03.340
These two were just trying
to capture the thief.

14:03.640 --> 14:07.480
Ms. Yamaguchi, you don't
actually believe that, do you?

14:07.610 --> 14:09.580
This is a very serious incident.

14:09.850 --> 14:14.190
We must hold a meeting as soon as
possible to discuss their expulsion.

14:14.350 --> 14:15.820
Go ahead, make my day!

14:15.920 --> 14:17.450
Expel me or whatever!

14:17.560 --> 14:18.580
Expel me too!

14:18.760 --> 14:20.590
I said hold on!

14:23.300 --> 14:24.560
Vice Principal...

14:24.700 --> 14:28.600
What are you going to do if
it turns out you're mistaken?

14:29.000 --> 14:31.100
There's no mistake about this.

14:31.540 --> 14:35.070
Now that would be a
"very serious incident", wouldn't it?

14:37.640 --> 14:39.310
Still, Ms. Yamaguchi.

14:39.410 --> 14:43.540
Should there be another incident,
the responsibility will fall on you!

14:43.920 --> 14:46.110
Of course. I'm ready to take it on.

14:46.350 --> 14:50.650
Well, perhaps there's room
for further evaluation.

14:50.760 --> 14:53.560
But remember, we can't
have any more trouble!

14:55.360 --> 14:56.420
Yankumi.

14:56.960 --> 14:58.360
Goddammit!

14:58.530 --> 15:01.430
Both the cops and the vice principal!
This is so screwed!

15:01.740 --> 15:02.460
All right.

15:02.570 --> 15:05.660
We're gonna find the real criminal,
if it's the last thing we do!

15:05.770 --> 15:06.360
Huh?

15:06.470 --> 15:08.910
Didn't he just tell you not
to cause any more trouble?

15:09.040 --> 15:10.100
I don't think we should...

15:10.240 --> 15:12.340
Shut up!
Who gives a rat's ass about that!

15:12.850 --> 15:15.580
Well, what do you have in mind?

15:16.220 --> 15:18.690
Hey, just leave it to me.

15:20.550 --> 15:22.250
Oh good evening, Ojou!

15:22.390 --> 15:23.980
Good to see you, Ojou!

15:24.320 --> 15:25.020
Hey!

15:25.190 --> 15:26.320
Welcome.

15:27.130 --> 15:30.060
Yasue Neesan, I have a favor to ask.

15:31.730 --> 15:33.670
Ask away.

15:33.900 --> 15:36.500
I'll do anything for you, Ojou.

15:36.670 --> 15:38.070
Right!

15:40.910 --> 15:44.070
No crap?
So that's what's going down now?

15:44.440 --> 15:45.940
Sounds pretty badass...

15:46.080 --> 15:47.310
...sting and nab!

15:47.780 --> 15:52.740
One of the thief's victims was a young
woman, so we figured it was doable.

15:52.850 --> 15:57.050
Yeah, but if it's a friend of Yankumi's,
maybe we shouldn't get our hopes up.

15:58.130 --> 15:59.820
But a sting operation...

15:59.930 --> 16:01.550
Yankumi came up with a good one.

16:02.700 --> 16:04.430
Thanks for waiting!

16:11.840 --> 16:12.740
You moron!

16:12.840 --> 16:14.170
You're the decoy?

16:14.640 --> 16:17.130
Well, I couldn't ask
anyone else to do this.

16:17.340 --> 16:19.510
Yeah, but did you have to go blond?

16:19.610 --> 16:21.380
Not to mention you're
wearing a track suit!

16:21.480 --> 16:23.040
Are you really serious about doing this?

16:23.520 --> 16:27.080
But when I got to my friend's house,
this was all she had left.

16:27.190 --> 16:28.950
What kind of friend is that?

16:29.560 --> 16:30.420
Don't worry!

16:30.860 --> 16:34.060
I also borrowed this expensive handbag,
so I'll look like a rich bitch!

16:35.500 --> 16:37.930
Even weirder. That combination.

16:38.030 --> 16:39.060
You think so?

16:42.440 --> 16:43.730
I think it'll be fine.

16:44.100 --> 16:45.540
Let's just do it.

16:57.920 --> 16:59.750
What's with that walk?

16:59.990 --> 17:02.790
I can't figure out
what role she's playing now.

17:02.960 --> 17:04.020
Hey!

17:04.790 --> 17:06.560
I got some food.

17:07.030 --> 17:08.690
Let's take a break.

17:08.800 --> 17:10.790
Huh? A break already?

17:11.060 --> 17:13.190
Well, I'm hungry, man.

17:13.700 --> 17:15.640
Looks real good.

17:16.570 --> 17:18.400
Hot! Hey Kuma!

17:18.570 --> 17:19.600
Oh, sorry.

17:21.540 --> 17:22.530
Hey, hey.

17:23.440 --> 17:25.540
We lost sight of Yankumi.
You think she's okay?

17:25.750 --> 17:26.940
Don't sweat it.

17:27.080 --> 17:30.610
There's no way anyone would go
near a woman who looks like that.

17:30.720 --> 17:32.480
Let's just eat.

17:37.990 --> 17:42.020
I guess he wouldn't appear so easily.

17:42.200 --> 17:43.690
Hey, Kathy.

17:43.830 --> 17:44.350
Huh?

17:49.740 --> 17:50.930
Kathy?

17:53.610 --> 17:55.130
Look, Kathy.

18:01.250 --> 18:02.410
Huh?

18:02.850 --> 18:04.480
Very unusual...

18:04.650 --> 18:06.810
So those freaks really do exist!

18:08.760 --> 18:09.980
Still...

18:10.860 --> 18:13.120
Are they really following me?

18:13.260 --> 18:16.490
Well, I do feel a presence, so
they must be around somewhere.

18:16.700 --> 18:19.030
Ojou, have no fear.

18:19.330 --> 18:22.060
I would give my life for you...

18:26.440 --> 18:27.500
Someone!

18:27.670 --> 18:28.900
Thief!

18:31.040 --> 18:32.410
Stop, dammit!

18:34.680 --> 18:35.980
Stop!

18:39.820 --> 18:41.980
Damn you, I said stop!

18:47.760 --> 18:48.560
Fuji!

18:51.670 --> 18:53.930
All right.
Don't move a muscle!

18:54.230 --> 18:55.930
Ow! Ow! Ow!

18:56.040 --> 18:57.940
Good job, Fuji!

18:58.410 --> 19:00.430
Piece of cake.

19:01.110 --> 19:03.170
Where they hell are they, anyway?

19:05.150 --> 19:07.810
Fuji, I want you to stay back, now...

19:11.520 --> 19:13.710
Help!

19:14.520 --> 19:17.250
Somebody! help me!

19:18.760 --> 19:19.380
Hey.

19:19.560 --> 19:21.190
Wasn't that Yamaguchi's voice?

19:21.290 --> 19:22.590
Huh? Are you sure?

19:24.000 --> 19:25.360
Hurry!

19:25.500 --> 19:26.190
Crap!

19:27.130 --> 19:28.930
Help!

19:29.040 --> 19:30.440
There! There she is!

19:30.540 --> 19:32.400
Yankumi! Is that the guy?

19:32.670 --> 19:33.500
Hurry!

19:33.670 --> 19:35.470
He's grabbing me by my arms!

19:35.580 --> 19:38.740
Hey, you're the one grabbing me!

19:39.810 --> 19:40.750
Hey!

19:41.510 --> 19:42.380
Crap!

19:42.480 --> 19:43.280
You scum!

19:43.380 --> 19:44.180
Take this!

19:44.280 --> 19:45.450
Go to hell!

19:50.120 --> 19:52.290
You're never gonna win an Oscar.

19:52.660 --> 19:54.390
What are you talking about?

19:54.530 --> 19:55.650
They saved me!

19:55.760 --> 19:58.700
Damn! Why does this one
always have to be so...

19:59.130 --> 20:00.570
Guys, you can get off him.

20:00.730 --> 20:02.430
He's not going anywhere.

20:03.640 --> 20:04.760
Kuma, you idiot, move!

20:04.870 --> 20:05.930
I can't breathe...

20:06.670 --> 20:07.540
Huh?

20:12.150 --> 20:14.340
So, is he a student from our school?

20:14.450 --> 20:15.640
No.

20:15.780 --> 20:18.980
Yeah, this guy isn't from our school.

20:19.120 --> 20:20.050
Are you sure?

20:20.150 --> 20:22.020
He might be from another grade.

20:22.190 --> 20:22.950
No.

20:23.120 --> 20:25.250
He's definitely not a
student from our school.

20:25.360 --> 20:26.290
I mean...

20:26.490 --> 20:28.550
He's not even a kid!

20:37.670 --> 20:41.000
We've had our name dragged
through the papers countless times...

20:41.110 --> 20:43.800
But never before in a positive light!

20:45.350 --> 20:46.750
I knew it!

20:47.080 --> 20:49.380
I knew it wasn't one of our students.

20:49.480 --> 20:51.450
Yeah, thank God!

20:51.650 --> 20:53.180
I'm so relieved.

20:53.450 --> 20:56.620
Yes, these kids are good boys at heart.

21:04.030 --> 21:07.970
Jeez, those guys made me proud.

21:08.200 --> 21:11.100
Yankumi, I heard you were the decoy.

21:11.240 --> 21:12.430
Nice going!

21:12.770 --> 21:13.900
No, no.

21:14.040 --> 21:16.770
If they hadn't saved me,
the thief would've decked me.

21:16.880 --> 21:18.670
Who knows what he would've done next!

21:18.780 --> 21:20.770
Uchiyama and the others
have balls, don't they?

21:22.050 --> 21:24.110
Hey, you little prick, Uchi!

21:24.220 --> 21:26.780
What's up with this?

21:26.990 --> 21:28.720
Huh? What are you talking about?

21:28.820 --> 21:30.520
Is something the matter, boys?

21:30.620 --> 21:32.020
Stop playing dumb!

21:32.390 --> 21:34.050
Oh, that...

21:34.990 --> 21:38.560
I told them it wasn't me, but...

21:38.670 --> 21:40.000
You bastard!

21:40.400 --> 21:42.800
Don't mess with us!
Who says you're our leader?

21:42.940 --> 21:44.030
You sleazebag!

21:44.140 --> 21:46.660
When the hell did you do this interview?

21:46.770 --> 21:48.260
Help!

22:07.030 --> 22:17.030
<i>We are all born</i>
<i>crying out to the world.</i>

22:18.100 --> 22:28.000
<i>Because of all the endless grief</i>
<i>that we must go through in life.</i>

22:28.820 --> 22:38.750
<i>All of the heartache</i>
<i>is such a heavy load to bear.</i>

22:38.930 --> 22:48.920
<i>On those days when I am alone and cold</i>
<i>I'll light a fire with my own two hands.</i>

22:49.470 --> 22:59.470
<i>Treacherous mountains are my chosen path.</i>
<i>I'll move forward without a backward glance.</i>

23:18.360 --> 23:20.560
See, I knew in my heart that...

23:20.670 --> 23:24.430
...there couldn't be such a
lowlife punk in Ojou's class.

23:25.140 --> 23:28.870
But Ojou, that blond hair is too much!

23:28.980 --> 23:32.540
Clad in an elegant kimono,
raven hair swept up...

23:32.650 --> 23:35.550
That's the Ojou we all want to see!

23:36.620 --> 23:39.140
Next episode: Ooedo Clan in Crisis!

23:39.290 --> 23:41.910
Time to get dressed up to the nines!

23:42.020 --> 23:45.360
<i>Ooedo Clan in Crisis!</i>
